---
description: Never bind to, kill, or replace user production servers (11434, 8081, etc.)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Production ports — hands off

The user runs **production** inference locally. Agents must not stop, replace, or compete with those processes.

## Reserved production ports (never touch)

| Port | Service | Who runs it |
|------|---------|-------------|
| **11434** | `./zerollama serve` (default `OLLAMA_HOST`) | **User** |
| **8081** | Python runtime sidecar (`ZEROLLAMA_RUNTIME_URL`, auto on Darwin serve) | **User** (via serve) |

Treat any `zerollama`, `ollama`, `llama-server`, or `runtime serve` listening on these ports as **production**. Do not kill, `pkill`, `kill`, `launchctl stop`, or `docker stop` them to “free” the port or “fix” a conflict.

If the user has other long-running servers they started (e.g. `llama-server` on a fixed port they chose), **do not stop those either** unless they explicitly say “kill my server on port X”.

## Never do this

- Start `zerollama serve`, `ollama serve`, or bind HTTP on **11434** or **8081**
- Set `OLLAMA_HOST` to `:11434` / `127.0.0.1:11434` when **starting** a server from the agent
- Set `ZEROLLAMA_RUNTIME_URL` to `:8081` when **starting** a sidecar from the agent (unless user asked for a dedicated lab sidecar on another port)
- **Kill or stop** any process listening on **11434** or **8081** (including Cursor, Ollama, zerollama, llama-server, Python runtime)
- Run `./zerollama serve` or `./scripts/build_zerollama_mac.sh && ./zerollama serve` in the background to “verify the build” without explicit user request
- Rebuild and auto-start serve on production ports after a code change

## When the agent must run servers (lab only)

Use **non-production** ports and state that in commands:

```bash
# zerollama lab
OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11435 ./zerollama serve

# runtime lab sidecar
ZEROLLAMA_RUNTIME_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18081 ./scripts/serve_mac_runtime.sh  # if script allows override

# llama-server subprocess smoke
--port 18082   # never 8081 or 11434
```

CI/smoke defaults (`:8080` Go, `:8081` sidecar) apply only inside **`./scripts/*_smoke.sh`** — not against the user’s daily `:11434` stack.

Prefer **read-only** checks against production when it is already up (`curl http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags`) instead of starting a second server.

## Port already in use

1. Report which port and process (e.g. `lsof -nP -iTCP:11434 -sTCP:LISTEN`) **read-only**
2. Ask the **user** to stop their server or pick a lab port for agent work
3. **Do not** kill the listener unless the user explicitly requests freeing that **specific** port

## Builds and tests

- `./scripts/build_zerollama_mac.sh` — build binary only; **do not** chain `./zerollama serve` on 11434
- Tests/smokes — bind lab ports (`11435`, `11499`, `8080`, `18081`, `18082`); never production ports
- If a test fails with “address already in use”, change the test port — **do not** kill production
